{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773183460,"nonce":"peNK4QvJC8GjU/jzOULnXc0zQy0=","title":"SimpleStagedNetwork.__call__ cannot execute LSTMCell — returns tuple, not array","message":"In feedbax/nn.py, SimpleStagedNetwork.__call__ passes the cell return value to hidden_nonlinearity and then the readout. GRUCell returns a plain array. But LSTMCell returns a tuple (output, (hidden, cell)). The nonlinearity application and readout will crash on a tuple. Despite LSTM appearing as an option in the Network component schema, it cannot actually be used. Fix: handle the LSTM tuple return in SimpleStagedNetwork, extracting the hidden state correctly.","files":null}]}